Subject: [PATCH 00/10] sparc32: guarded HyperSPARC maintenance optimizations (HOLD)

I am keeping these ten optimizations on hold. They follow the generic
and HyperSPARC correctness series. Geometry guards, VM_PFNMAP coverage,
interface choices and a fresh matched hardware comparison remain pending.

I completed a native GDB 18.1 build on a dual-CPU HyperSPARC RT626
SPARCstation 20 with 512 MB RAM and a native SPARC32 SMP kernel containing
the combined fixes and optimizations, plus separate platform prerequisites.
I observed no core dumps, livelock or new kernel messages during the run.
This validates the combined integration, not each patch in isolation.
This run does not establish performance gains or resolve those concerns.

Magnus Lindholm (10):
  sparc32: isolate the HyperSPARC kmap whole-cache sweep
  sparc32: avoid no-op HyperSPARC DMA cross-calls
  sparc32: demap HyperSPARC kmap_local TLB entries by page
  sparc32: track highmem pages exposed through vmap
  sparc32: avoid redundant HyperSPARC kmap flushes
  sparc32: narrow safe HyperSPARC kmap unmap flushes
  sparc32: avoid duplicate publication of HyperSPARC highmem copies
  sparc32: unroll the HyperSPARC combined cache sweep eight ways
  sparc32: narrow guarded HyperSPARC copy-source unmaps
  sparc32: reduce arithmetic in the HyperSPARC combined cache sweep

